         <editionStmt>
            <p>The following passages from the Chronicle of 1234 are all those introduced as quotations of the third part of the Ecclesiastical History (henceforth EH) of John of Ephesus. Passages which can serve to close gaps in the EH's sole manuscript have also been included. Silvio Roggo identified the passages based on a comparison of the Chronicle to the EH and transcribed them from the edition of the Chronicle. The list of testimonies found in Jan van Ginkel's dissertation (pp. 237-240) provided an important point of comparison, as did the edition of the EH by E.W. Brooks. This is an exact copy of the Syriac text found in Chabot's 1916-1920 edition of the Chronicle, based on its only manuscript, now lost. The Syriac text was proofread by Philip Michael Forness.</p>
         </editionStmt>
