            <listWit>
               <head>Manuscript Witnesses</head>
               <witness xml:id="MS1234">
                  <abbr type="siglum">MS1234</abbr>
                  <name>Manuscript of the Chronicle of 1234 (lost)</name>
                  <origDate>end of 14th century</origDate>
                  <locus>Chabot, pp. 213 (vol. 1); 244-257 (vol. 2)</locus>
                  <note>Chabot's edition was based on a copy of the manuscript he received from Ephrem Barsaum. Chabot himself did not have direct access to the manuscript. In a couple places in the text encoded in the present file, Chabot deviated from the copy he received from Barsaum as noted. References to the manuscript should be understood as references to the transcription of Barsaum used by Chabot. The description of the manuscript, based on the information Chabot received from Barsaum, can be found in vol. 2 of his edition, pp. ii-v.</note>
               </witness>
            </listWit>
